      "writtenOn": "2022-02-22T10:41:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think you actually need to start a rematch.\n\nConsider this scenario :\n• Wifi A connects and starts satisfying the default request\n• A request is filed for a different Wifi band. Wifi B connects and satisfies the request for a different band, and could satisfy the default request but it doesn\u0027t because it\u0027s newer than Wifi A.\n• Wifi A is marked as pending replacement.\n\nIn this situation, Wifi B will immediately start beating Wifi A so strictly speaking we should be rematching. I get that it\u0027s not the end of the world if we don\u0027t, considering we should see a replacement soon and even if we don\u0027t we\u0027ll timeout Wifi A soon, but I don\u0027t like too much the result that transitions will depend on whether anything else happens to trigger a rematch during the timeout.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3662,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 3662,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "5ad2ff1dd351367315214f96dd179d9287880f69",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
